Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix:=20chart=20only=20visibly=20moving=20on=201?=
 =?UTF-8?q?m=20=E2=80=94=20Y-axis=20scale,=20not=20a=20data=20bug?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every timeframe seeds ~300 bars of history (see _seedSymbolHistory in
engine.js) — fine for 1m (5 hours), but fitContent() zoomed the chart
out to show ALL of it on every timeframe: 1d showed ~300 DAYS, 4h
showed ~50 days, 1h showed ~12.5 days. Against a price axis scaled to
weeks/months of history, a single tick's few-cent wiggle in the
currently-forming bar was a sub-pixel change — invisible, even though
the underlying data was updating correctly every second (verified:
tick() already updates every timeframe's candles in engine.js, and a
quick live measurement showed real ~/bin/sh.05-0.2 per-tick movement).

Fix: show only the most recent ~120 bars by default instead of the
full seeded history (standard behavior for any real trading UI
anyway), so the visible price range stays tight enough for live ticks
to actually be visible on 1m/5m/15m/1h/4h. 1d will still look calmer
by comparison, which is expected — no real exchange's daily candle
visibly wiggles second-to-second either.
---
 public/dashboard.html | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/public/dashboard.html b/public/dashboard.html
index 7503c0e..3700f17 100644
--- a/public/dashboard.html
+++ b/public/dashboard.html
@@ -545,7 +545,21 @@ async function loadCandles(){
       candleSeries.setData(toChartBars(candleData));
       volumeSeries.setData(toVolumeBars(candleData));
     }
-    chart.timeScale().fitContent();
+    // ROOT CAUSE of "only 1m looks alive": every timeframe seeds ~300 bars of
+    // history (300min for 1m, but 300 DAYS for 1d, 50 days for 4h, etc — see
+    // _seedSymbolHistory in engine.js). fitContent() used to zoom out to show
+    // ALL of it, so on anything above 1m the visible price axis spanned weeks
+    // or months — a single tick's few-cent wiggle in the last bar became a
+    // sub-pixel change against that scale, invisible even though the data was
+    // updating correctly every second. Showing only the most recent ~120 bars
+    // (standard for any real trading UI anyway) keeps the visible range tight
+    // enough that live ticks are actually visible on every timeframe.
+    const VISIBLE_BARS = 120;
+    if (candleData.length > VISIBLE_BARS) {
+      chart.timeScale().setVisibleLogicalRange({ from: candleData.length - VISIBLE_BARS, to: candleData.length + 2 });
+    } else {
+      chart.timeScale().fitContent();
+    }
     updateOHLC();
   }catch(e){
     // Keep the last good chart on screen rather than clearing it to nothing.
